# The dev tooling and the hardware-test procedure are project knowledge and are tracked;
# whatever else Claude leaves here is not. `.claude/*` and not `.claude/` on purpose: git
# does not descend into a directory it has ignored whole, so a negation inside one never
# fires - which is why the re-inclusion the tools README has always claimed did nothing,
# and why those tools were lost once already.
.claude/*
!.claude/tools/
!.claude/skills/
# Generated, and built on demand. The sources and build-status.json are the tracked half.
.claude/tools/bin/
.claude/tools/build-status.html
.hermes/
CLAUDE.md
# UI reference snapshots — third-party imagery, design reference only (see the folder's README)
ui-snapshots-inspiration/

# Generated by resources/web/print_processing/mockups/build_standalone.py - half a
# megabyte of inlined copies of files that are already in the tree, regenerated in one
# command. Committing it would churn on every mockup edit and could silently drift from
# what run_webkit.py actually drives.
resources/web/print_processing/mockups/multiace-standalone.html
resources/web/print_processing/mockups/multiace-g-standalone.html
